                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a095b319-c0a8-3e73-bf0d-c85ac95e7371",
                        "entry_id": "1f6dd3f0-1c53-3fb9-a50c-fd43f2c1ecfd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "żebrzący ascetyczny mnich muzułmański"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f7bca70-5d39-4002-88b1-87538c641529",
                                "sense_id": "a095b319-c0a8-3e73-bf0d-c85ac95e7371",
                                "text": "Domeną fakira jest chodzenie boso po rozżarzonych węglach."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "769b8e6d-ecd6-42a4-9a7e-ef1b6d1d3079",
                        "source_entry_id": "1f6dd3f0-1c53-3fb9-a50c-fd43f2c1ecfd",
                        "source_sense_id": "a095b319-c0a8-3e73-bf0d-c85ac95e7371",
                        "target_lang_word": "fakir",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fakir",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e39dd497-70a6-3067-837f-cb4a50700c12",
                                        "entry_id": "a6be1692-8b18-30f3-b59c-a378c9bc5bd5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A faqir, owning no personal property and usually living solely off alms."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea0119f3-5cf1-323b-98d7-8432f3ebf76a",
                                        "entry_id": "a6be1692-8b18-30f3-b59c-a378c9bc5bd5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An ascetic mendicant, especially one who performs feats of endurance or apparent magic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Hinduism"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2e319aa-9efa-4cde-a806-03183c43774b",
                                                "sense_id": "ea0119f3-5cf1-323b-98d7-8432f3ebf76a",
                                                "text": "The preposterous altruism too![…]Resist not evil. It is an insane immolation of self—as bad intrinsically as fakirs stabbing themselves or anchorites warping their spines in caves scarcely large enough for a fair-sized dog."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "93232b6f-544b-36ea-ac77-84c6bf81dc89",
                                        "entry_id": "a6be1692-8b18-30f3-b59c-a378c9bc5bd5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who takes advantage of the gullible through fakery, especially of a spiritual or religious nature."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3eb0247-2570-4617-8256-59fb694f8d64",
                                                "sense_id": "93232b6f-544b-36ea-ac77-84c6bf81dc89",
                                                "text": "He denounces no one until he has all the damaging facts in hand, very frequently backed up with affidavits. He 'Lawsonized' certain stock jobbers and financial fakirs of London before the Boston advertising man was heard of."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "325e5988-ace8-4ca0-8cdd-2550445cbe3e",
                                                "sense_id": "93232b6f-544b-36ea-ac77-84c6bf81dc89",
                                                "text": "\"But a stranger who had come up to the group just at this point, when they were pronouncing the soup delicious, laughed aloud. \"'What a set of fools you all are!' he cried. 'This tramp is just a fakir. That stone had nothing to do with the soup.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7b2cd59-51f9-424c-bb3c-eca249eb4d69",
                                                "sense_id": "93232b6f-544b-36ea-ac77-84c6bf81dc89",
                                                "text": "He was, as the undercover agent concluded, a fabulous raconteur or, as one other person summed him up, \"a monumental fakir and liar.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8c5c1b4-318c-4e20-9c5e-7f3723c7ffc7",
                                                "sense_id": "93232b6f-544b-36ea-ac77-84c6bf81dc89",
                                                "text": "From what I hear of him he's a fakir, and I won't encourage him in his attempts to get into society at my expense."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e737b963-c537-4d65-b7e9-6b7840b78f61",
                        "source_entry_id": "1f6dd3f0-1c53-3fb9-a50c-fd43f2c1ecfd",
                        "source_sense_id": "a095b319-c0a8-3e73-bf0d-c85ac95e7371",
                        "target_lang_word": "fakir",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fakir",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "76094b0d-9918-35b4-9056-cfb6af572674",
                                        "entry_id": "4ebef280-6241-3aa6-891c-108b1affced2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ascète soufi, derviche musulman qui court le pays en vivant d’aumônes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9bd80997-6fdc-301d-937f-2bd55e5fa255",
                                        "entry_id": "4ebef280-6241-3aa6-891c-108b1affced2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mystique hindou."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6087790-cafa-462d-939b-1b99dbec0a5c",
                                                "sense_id": "9bd80997-6fdc-301d-937f-2bd55e5fa255",
                                                "text": "Du fond de la ville, je vis l’automne qui rougissait les arbres et verdissait les pâturages, et le jour où le collège se rouvrit, j’y ramenai comme à l’ordinaire un être agité, malheureux, une sorte d’esprit plié en deux, comme un fakir attristé qui s’examine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97c555f4-1726-477f-9e92-9eeed184259c",
                                                "sense_id": "9bd80997-6fdc-301d-937f-2bd55e5fa255",
                                                "text": "C'était un fakir, à demi nu, de la couleur du bronze, et dont la physionomie impassible semblait ne connaître ni la douleur ni le plaisir."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe14bd3a-940c-48b1-bbe8-802529618fea",
                                                "sense_id": "9bd80997-6fdc-301d-937f-2bd55e5fa255",
                                                "text": "Il était assis, figé dans une immobilité absolue et impressionnante, à la manière d'un fakir."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "621a9ea7-f677-387d-baf3-518b4d7e6a52",
                                        "entry_id": "4ebef280-6241-3aa6-891c-108b1affced2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Saltimbanque ou illusionniste pseudo-oriental, sans aucune référence ou différence religieuse, qui exécute des exercices physiques pénibles et des tours extraordinaires attribués à un pouvoir surnaturel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b3d5cbb-98e7-4e91-90fe-ce00cc6e21e8",
                                                "sense_id": "621a9ea7-f677-387d-baf3-518b4d7e6a52",
                                                "text": "Un numéro de fakir."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
